   "text": {
    "L1": "Panchayati Raj is local self-government in villages.",
    "L2": "It has three tiers, from the village level to the district level.",
    "L3": "The gram sabha includes every adult aged 18 or above whose name is on the voters' list.",
    "L4": "The gram sabha discusses plans, checks the panchayat's work and helps choose scheme beneficiaries.",
    "L5": "The gram panchayat has elected panch members and a sarpanch.",
    "L6": "It looks after needs such as drinking water, roads, drains, street lights and cleanliness.",
    "L7": "The gram panchayat is elected for five years, while a government-appointed secretary keeps records.",
    "L8": "The three tiers are gram panchayat, panchayat samiti and zila parishad."
   },
